To decompose the mission into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we will define goals and tasks with their respective hierarchical structure, runtime annotations, and relationships. Below is the structured breakdown:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Name       | Text                                                                                     | Runtime       | Goal Type   | Relation |
|------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------|-------------|----------|
| **G1**     | Deliver food to inpatient room                                                          | #             | Perform     | AND      |
| **G2**     | Determine delivery method                                                               | FALLBACK(G3, G4) | Achieve     | OR       |
| **G3**     | Deliver food directly to room table                                                     | -             | Achieve     | -        |
| **G4**     | Coordinate tray retrieval                                                               | FALLBACK(G5, G6) | Achieve     | OR       |
| **G5**     | Retrieve food with inpatient assistance                                                 | -             | Achieve     | -        |
| **G6**     | Retrieve food with robot or human cooperation                                           | FALLBACK(G7, G8) | Achieve     | OR       |
| **G7**     | Coordinate between robots                                                               | -             | Achieve     | -        |
| **G8**     | Coordinate between robot and human (nurse, companion)                                   | -             | Achieve     | -        |
| **G9**     | Track meal retrieval details                                                            | #             | Perform     | AND      |
| **G10**    | Alert if wrong meal is retrieved                                                        | -             | Perform     | -        |
| **G11**    | Retrieve dirty dishes from room                                                         | #             | Perform     | AND      |
| **G12**    | Determine dish retrieval method                                                         | FALLBACK(G13, G14) | Achieve     | OR       |
| **G13**    | Retrieve dishes unassisted                                                              | -             | Achieve     | -        |
| **G14**    | Coordinate dish retrieval with robot or human                                           | FALLBACK(G15, G16) | Achieve     | OR       |
| **G15**    | Coordinate between robots                                                               | -             | Achieve     | -        |
| **G16**    | Coordinate between robot and human (nurse, companion)                                   | -             | Achieve     | -        |

#### Tasks

| Name      | Text                                                                                   | Relation | Location   | Number of Robots |
|-----------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------|------------------|
| **AT1**   | Navigate to inpatient room                                                            | AND      | Hospital   | [1]              |
| **AT2**   | Deliver food to room table                                                             | AND      | Room Table | [1]              |
| **AT3**   | Indicate meal retrieval                                                                | AND      | Inpatient  | [1]              |
| **AT4**   | Track meal retrieval details                                                           | AND      | System     | [1]              |
| **AT5**   | Alert wrong meal retrieval                                                             | AND      | System     | [1]              |
| **AT6**   | Navigate to room for dish retrieval                                                    | AND      | Hospital   | [1]              |
| **AT7**   | Retrieve dishes unassisted                                                             | AND      | Room       | [1]              |
| **AT8**   | Coordinate dish retrieval with robot                                                   | AND      | Room       | [2]              |
| **AT9**   | Coordinate dish retrieval with human                                                   | AND      | Room       | [1, 1]           |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G9, G11 [AND][parallel]**
- **G2 -> G3, G4 [OR][FALLBACK]**
- **G4 -> G5, G6 [OR][FALLBACK]**
- **G6 -> G7, G8 [OR][FALLBACK]**
- **G9 -> AT3, AT4 [AND][parallel]**
- **G10 -> AT5 [AND]**
- **G11 -> G12, G13, G14 [AND][parallel]**
- **G12 -> G13, G14 [OR][FALLBACK]**
- **G14 -> G15, G16 [OR][FALLBACK]**

### Summary

This goal model provides a structured approach to the mission, breaking it down into actionable tasks and ensuring flexibility in handling uncertainties and cooperation requirements. The use of OR and AND decompositions allows for efficient execution and adaptability in dynamic environments.
